			N	7024414	A	Province of the ancient Roman Empire. The emperor Diocletian (284-305 CE), in his reorganization of the empire, formed two provinces, Byzacena and Tripolitania, from the southern and eastern parts of the old province of Africa. Tripolitania included the western part of Libya. The capital was Leptis Magna.	1		7030341
